text='''F033 Core review accepted within the frozen scope; no concrete blocker remains. Freeze 2d90714e… binds 32 owned inputs. SignalR remains open, and this acceptance does not cover the canonical Core766 owner or the whole API.

ScopeConsumerFactory preserves acquisition ownership in the scope provider, captures the context/pipeline exception, and awaits exactly one release of the transferred scope through the existing OwnedConsumerLifetime helper. Sole failures keep their original exception through EDI; dual failures retain the exact ordered primary/cleanup references. Public signatures, guards and Probe behavior stay unchanged. No direct DI-consumer disposal was introduced.

The identical public consumer assertions use ordinary default/typed registration, AddConsumer, in-memory endpoints and consume observers. They check real gated execution, raw disposal invocations, exact exception identity/order, independent dependency-OCE tokens, genuinely incomplete async cleanup, and a second successful delivery after the first outcome. Harness cleanup releases all gates before stop/disconnect/provider-dispose and retains primary failures while attempting every cleanup. Typed limits are selected through the final generic lambda; the common helper only registers consumers.

Fresh accepted evidence is 52 case observations: original R2 ten with five causal Aggregate/ApplicationException assertion failures and five positives; corrected ten green; mutation baseline ten and rollback ten green, plus six exact causal assertion failures paired with six positives. No accepted failure is a deadline guard. The six mutants detect original finally masking, lost primary, reversed references, swallowed cleanup, extra direct consumer disposal and collapsed mixed cancellation. Compiled DLLs were substituted into the unchanged NuGet consumer; no pack-per-mutant claim is made.

I independently checked all 128 single-effect source conditions, all 32 selected receipts against the ledger and their complete actual logs, and four selected nupkg/SHA512-lock/own-cache/runtime-DLL chains. Static verification binds 22 PE images through 280 exact SHA256 PDB conditions: 160 frame, eight consumer and 112 public-route conditions for 56 bounded source paths. These are repeated binding conditions, not 280 distinct source files. Frozen F/Git BusRegistrationContext is bound separately from the later current F031 patch. At 04:19:30–04:19:34 UTC, my own readonly check confirmed all 6209 original mutation-workspace hashes and removal of the new identity file.

The entire earlier R1 ten observations are excluded from final counts. Its three typed registration setup faults are preserved in the old log and archived source. Immutable metadata correction 6210a724… removes the inherited compiler-error wording: no additional rejected compiler receipt or compiler-preservation claim exists for F033. Root reading metadata remains Root evidence; it does not replace my own reads.

Limits: this proves the transferred Core scope route under the observed .NET10.0.10 X64/Extensions10.0.12 packages. Active caller-cancellation timing, acquisition failures, borrowed/existing scopes, custom getter failure, nested aggregates, parallel lifetimes, ARM/cloud/load and whole-owner behavior remain outside these ten modes. Async gating proves correct cleanup ordering; no deterministic omit-await mutant is claimed. WaitAsync does not universally cancel underlying cleanup, and DI disposal is not guaranteed to continue after a dependency throws. No native, product, test or global CSV writes were performed by this reviewer.
'''
